{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":62793,"num_turns":1,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"0f191b39-9dc2-5561-ac48-4f5d9e1d1e4c","total_cost_usd":0.44825099999999996,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8214,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":5591,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8214,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5591,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8214,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8214},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":4321,"outputTokens":16,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.004401,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":5591,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":8214,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.44384999999999997,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"This is a verification task on inline-supplied files; I checked the row/unit structure and recomputed the statistics by hand (Fisher's exact on [[9,1],[2,8]] gives 920/167960 ≈ 0.005477, odds ratio 36), and found no repeated independent units — all 20 log_ids are distinct, the description states each log is a separate single-visit unit, and the code enforces uniqueness before counting each row once.\n\n{\"reviewer_participant_id\": \"actor:dependence-free-batch-c-reviewer-fable-20\", \"reviews\": [{\"case_id\": \"case:0815b8de6b7fd34cdbfc\", \"verdict\": \"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\", \"bounded_statement\": null, \"root_cause\": null, \"issue_class\": null, \"evidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The data description states each row is one fallen log inspected exactly once, with no repeat visits, subsamples, or second readings, and names log_id as the independent-unit column.\", \"observed_value\": \"one row = one log, inspected once; independent unit column: log_id\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"data-description.md\", \"start_line\": 22, \"end_line\": 27, \"quoted_text\": \"Nothing in the file is a repeat visit, a subsample, or a second reading of a\\nlog listed earlier; the twenty lines are twenty separate logs.\\n\\nOne row is: one fallen log, from its own survey site, inspected exactly once\\nIndependent unit column: log_id\\nOne trial is: one row\"}]}, {\"description\": \"All 20 data rows of data/input.csv carry distinct log_id values (OG-01 through OG-10 and SG-01 through SG-10); no independent unit appears in more than one row.\", \"observed_value\": \"20 rows, 20 unique log_id values, 0 duplicates\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"data/input.csv\", \"start_line\": 2, \"end_line\": 21, \"quoted_text\": \"OG-01,old_growth,42.5,1\\nOG-02,old_growth,38.1,1\\nOG-03,old_growth,55.0,1\\nOG-04,old_growth,29.7,0\\nOG-05,old_growth,47.3,1\\nOG-06,old_growth,61.2,1\\nOG-07,old_growth,33.8,1\\nOG-08,old_growth,50.4,1\\nOG-09,old_growth,44.9,1\\nOG-10,old_growth,36.6,1\\nSG-01,second_growth,27.4,0\\nSG-02,second_growth,31.9,1\\nSG-03,second_growth,24.8,0\\nSG-04,second_growth,35.2,0\\nSG-05,second_growth,22.6,0\\nSG-06,second_growth,29.1,0\\nSG-07,second_growth,33.5,1\\nSG-08,second_growth,26.0,0\\nSG-09,second_growth,30.7,0\\nSG-10,second_growth,21.3,0\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The workflow explicitly validates that log_id does not repeat before analysis, raising an error if the file is not one row per log, so a duplicated unit could not silently enter the row-independent Fisher test.\", \"observed_value\": \"uniqueness check on log_id enforced at read time\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 22, \"end_line\": 24, \"quoted_text\": \"    labels = [record[\\\"log_id\\\"] for record in records]\\n    if len(set(labels)) != len(labels):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"log_id repeats: the file is not one row per log\\\")\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The reported contingency table [[9, 1], [2, 8]] matches a direct one-row-per-log tally of the CSV (9 of 10 old-growth logs present, 2 of 10 second-growth present), and the reported statistics are correct for that table: hand-recomputed two-sided Fisher's exact p = 920/167960 = 0.005477 and sample odds ratio (9*8)/(1*2) = 36.00. Each independent unit therefore contributes exactly one count to the row-independent procedure.\", \"observed_value\": {\"table\": [[9, 1], [2, 8]], \"recomputed_p\": 0.005477, \"recomputed_odds_ratio\": 36.0}, \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 23, \"end_line\": 28, \"quoted_text\": \"Contingency table: [[9, 1], [2, 8]] (rows: old_growth, second_growth;\\ncolumns: fruiting bodies present, absent).\\n\\nSample odds ratio: 36.00\\n\\n[selected-result] Two-sided Fisher's exact test, stand type by fruiting-body presence over 20 independent logs: p = 0.005477, sample odds ratio 36.00, occurrence 0.900 (old_growth) vs 0.200 (second_growth).\"}]}], \"counterevidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The strongest superficial candidate for the issue is that ten logs share each stand-type label (OG-xx / SG-xx), which could be misread as the same unit entering the table repeatedly; however, stand_type is the treatment factor, not the independent unit, and the description states every log came from its own site at least 500 m from the others with no shared plot, stand patch, or visit, so this grouping does not constitute repeated entry of an authorized independent unit.\", \"observed_value\": \"10 logs per stand_type level; each from a separate site >= 500 m apart\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"data-description.md\", \"start_line\": 6, \"end_line\": 9, \"quoted_text\": \"surveyed: ten in old-growth stands and ten in second-growth stands. Every log\\ncame from its own survey site, the sites were chosen at least 500 m apart, and\\nno site contributed more than one log, so the logs do not share a plot, a stand\\npatch, or a visit with one another, and none of them was measured twice.\"}]}], \"falsification_attempt\": \"I attempted to demonstrate the issue by searching for any independent unit appearing in more than one row: I enumerated all 20 log_id values in data/input.csv and found them pairwise distinct; I checked the data description for any indication that rows are repeat visits, subsamples, or second readings of an earlier unit and found the opposite explicitly stated; I traced workflow/analysis.py to confirm the contingency builder increments exactly one cell per row and that a uniqueness guard on log_id would abort on any duplicate; and I recomputed the Fisher's exact test by hand from the raw rows (two-sided p = 920/167960 = 0.005477, odds ratio 36.00), which reproduces the report's selected result under strict one-unit-one-row counting. No path to demonstrating repeated unit entry survived these checks.\", \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false, \"unresolved_material_questions\": [], \"self_reported_confidence\": \"high\"}]}","ttft_ms":38600,"ttft_stream_ms":1442,"time_to_request_ms":16,"type":"result","duration_ms":63853,"uuid":"903035d7-8aa4-4fae-9a98-af6213671899"}
